data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"**Redis** gives sub-millisecond reads, TTL-based expiry that suits abandoned carts, and a simple model, but it adds a service to run and back up, and carts can be lost on eviction unless persistence is configured. **Postgres** keeps carts durable across restarts, makes abandoned-cart reporting a plain query, and needs no new infrastructure if you already run it. Its costs are slightly slower writes on each cart change and a cleanup job for expired carts. Either way, the cookie would hold only an opaque cart ID.\n\nI recommend **Postgres** unless you already operate Redis and expect very high cart-write volume. The decision is yours, so I've recorded it as ask **A1** with \"Use Postgres (Recommended)\" and \"Use Redis\" buttons. I haven't read or changed any files."}}

